"""Create shareable notes for the measured curve and stability screen."""
import csv,json,pathlib,statistics
R=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
model=json.loads((R/'curve.json').read_text());m=model['metrics']
stability=list(csv.DictReader((R/'low-level-stability.csv').open()))
lines=['# Fixture SD ELCO Koto SD / RA3 measurement','', 'Measured on October 5, 2026.','', 'The sensor was taped in place with its optical opening uncovered. No sensor coefficients, scaling, or offsets were calibrated against this fixture or ELCO specifications.','', '## Files','', '- `curve.csv`: all 100 dimmer settings, measured ascending/descending CCT and lux, monotonic lookup CCT, and variation flags.', '- `raw-readings.csv`: individual MQTT capture windows, including unmodified sensor CCT, x/y chromaticity, lux average/minimum/maximum, sample counts, request IDs, and UTC timestamps.', '- `low-level-stability.csv`: temporal output variation for every ascending 1% setting and descending checks.', '- `curve.json`: machine-readable lookup and repeatability metrics.', '- `curve.png` and `curve.pdf`: exportable plots.','', '## Method and limits','', 'At each ascending 1% setting, wait 3 seconds after the command and request two consecutive 20-reading windows. The firmware samples at approximately 125 ms spacing with 100 ms conversion settings: approximately five seconds of sensor sampling per setting, plus API/MQTT overhead. Descending checks repeat each 1% setting from 20% down to 1% and every 5% above 20%. A 60-second full-output warm-up precedes each capture segment.','', 'The firmware publishes only each window’s mean/minimum/maximum, not its individual lux waveform. These data can reveal slow output instability. They do not measure flicker frequency, PstLM, SVM, or certified percent flicker. Fast modulation can be averaged out by the sensor exposures; visual checking is required to confirm the absence of visible flicker.','', 'The `stability_screen` / `sensor_variation_screen` uses an explicitly chosen 5% repeatability screen: a window peak-to-peak range divided by its mean, or the spread of consecutive window means divided by their mean, above 5% is flagged. This threshold is not a flicker safety standard. `smoothed_modulation_percent` is 100 × (max−min)/(max+min) of the exposure-averaged measurements; it is not a high-speed flicker measurement.','', 'CCT is independently recomputed from the measured x/y coordinates by nearest distance in CIE 1960 u,v to a Planckian locus generated with CIE 1931 2° observer values (5 nm integration, 1 K search grid, second radiation constant 0.014388 m K). This avoids relying on the firmware’s McCamy approximation below its documented 2000 K range. Averaging and monotonic pooling stabilize the lookup; all original values remain in the CSVs. The 1 K calculation grid is not a claim of 1 K absolute sensor accuracy.','', 'Illuminance is local lux at the sensor, not fixture lumens or a normalized percentage of rated light output. The dimmer setting, optical geometry, driver, fixture, and any RA3 trims all contribute to this installation curve. No traceable reference-meter accuracy calibration was performed.','', 'Dark captures were incomplete or lacked valid chromaticity. Returned dark lux values are retained as `reported_lux`, but no invalid capture is treated as an exact zero or used for CCT. Ambient subtraction was not performed.','', '## Results','', '```json',json.dumps(m,indent=2),'```','', '## Data provenance','', '- Sensor: ESP32 / OPT4048, MQTT `lighting/calibrator/measurement`.', '- Dimmer entity: [omitted from publication].', '- Observer values: [Colour Science CIE standard observer dataset](https://github.com/colour-science/colour/blob/develop/colour/colorimetry/datasets/cmfs.py), with licence saved alongside source.', '- Observer definition: [CIE 1931 colour-matching functions, 2 degree observer](https://cie.co.at/datatable/cie-1931-colour-matching-functions-2-degree-observer).', '- Sensor/transform: [TI OPT4048](https://www.ti.com/product/OPT4048).', '- Firmware CCT approximation: [Adafruit OPT4048 library](https://github.com/adafruit/Adafruit_OPT4048/blob/master/Adafruit_OPT4048.cpp).','', 'Earlier runs are excluded: `preliminary-unsecured`, `fixed-sensor-initial-protocol`, and `tape-obstructed-check`.','']
(R/'README.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
